          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            the
            %em Stückelberg-Petermann renormalization group
            (
            %a{:href => "#StiecelbergPetermann53"}> Stückelberg-Petermann 53
            ) is the (original) incarnation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+group"} renormalization group
            in the perspective of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StueckelbergPetermannRenormalizationGroup"}
            below) of perturbative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction+vertex+redefinitions"} interaction vertex redefinitions
            (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InteractionVertexRedefinition"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-matrix"} S-matrix
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+schemes"} renormalization schemes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}, \mathcal{S}'
            are related by a unique
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+redefinition"} vertex redefinition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒵
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{Z}
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/precomposition"} precomposition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo ′
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi 𝒵
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{S}'
                  \\;=\;
                  \\mathcal{S} \circ \mathcal{Z}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This statement (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AnyTwoSMatrixRenormalizationSchemesDifferByAUniqueVertexRedefinition"}
            below) is also called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/main+theorem+of+perturbative+renormalization"} main theorem of perturbative renormalization
          %p
            If
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scaling+transformations"} scaling transformations
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            happen to transform
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+schemes"} renormalization schemes
            into each other, then this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/main+theorem+of+perturbative+renormalization"} main theorem of perturbative renormalization
            (prop.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AnyTwoSMatrixRenormalizationSchemesDifferByAUniqueVertexRedefinition"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scaling+transformation"} scaling transformation
            uniquely corresponds to a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction+vertex+redefinition"} interaction vertex redefinition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+redefinitions"} vertex redefinitions
            are given as funcitons of scale. As such they are also referred to as
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/running+coupling+constants"} running coupling constants
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GellMannLowTransformations"}
            below). Beware that these do not in general form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            but a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cocycle"} group cocycle
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gell-Mann-Low+renormalization+cocycle"} Gell-Mann-Low renormalization cocycle
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CocyclePropertyOfRunningCouplingConstants"}
            below.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The elements of the Stückelberg-Petermann renormalization group are
            %em
              perturbative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction+vertex+redefinitions"} interaction vertex redefinitions
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InteractionVertexRedefinition"}
            below). These
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} act
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-matrix"} S-matrix
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+schemes"} ("re"-)normalization schemes
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/precomposition"} precomposition
            (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CausalFactorizationSatisfiedByCompositionOfSMatrixWithVertexRedefinition"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+action"} transitive
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AnyTwoSMatrixRenormalizationSchemesDifferByAUniqueVertexRedefinition"}
            below). In this way these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+redefinitions"} vertex redefinitions
            translate between different choices of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} ("re"-)normalization
            %em Stückelerg-Petermann renormalization group
            (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StueckelbergPetermannRenormalizationGroup"}
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
