            %p
              Similarly the condition “field independence” follows immediately from the assumoption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}'
              satisfy this condition.
            %p
              It only remains to see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Z
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z_k
              indeed takes values in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+observables"} local observables
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-ordered+products"} time-ordered products
              a priori take values in the larrger space of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/microcausal+polynomial+observables"} microcausal polynomial observables
              this means to show that the spacetime support of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Z
                      %mi k
